MIT License (text: src/glmbench/tasks/_vendor/rnagym/LICENSE). The DMS assays (also
MIT) are fetched from upstream, not redistributed.

Cite: Notin et al., "RNAGym: Large-scale Benchmarks for RNA Fitness and Structure
Prediction", bioRxiv 2025.06.16.660049.

Individual DMS assays retain their original primary-publication citations (e.g.,
Firnberg et al. 2014 and Jacquier et al. 2013 for BLAT_ECOLX).

The subset used here is the 11 assays with RNA_TYPE == "mRNA-coding" and
ASSAY_DESCRIPTION == "PROK" in reference_sheet_final.csv: every assay of a
protein-coding gene from a prokaryote that RNAGym lists. The per-assay CSVs are
populated by scripts/fetch_rnagym_prok.py and pinned by sha256 in
prok_coding_manifest.yaml.

